Subject: [PATCH] platform: publish stock OpenWrt BSS settings through native UCI ownership

Use bounded native publication for Controller roles, credentials, new APs,
teardown and channel settings. Preserve pending writers and native netifd
ownership. Observe live security and beacon state before completion; config_id
alone is insufficient. Synchronize BSS descriptors and retire replaced HAL owners.

Use standard wlan<N> names for real AP endpoints and preserve their physical
radio ownership. This backend publishes supported AP roles; it does not add
STA-only radio inventory or dedicated-backhaul topology support. Generated
hostapd files and direct channel commands have no competing owner.

